Refactored the API to use the immutable matrix type as the boundary instead of raw `int[][]` snapshots.

What changed:
- Added display support to [`IntSquareMatrix.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/024_floyd_warshall/IntSquareMatrix.java#L1-L78) with `toDisplayString()` and `toString()`.
- Changed [`WeightedGraph.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/024_floyd_warshall/WeightedGraph.java#L1-L52) so `adjacencyMatrix()` now returns an immutable `IntSquareMatrix`.
- Changed [`AllPairsShortestPaths.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/024_floyd_warshall/AllPairsShortestPaths.java#L1-L63) so `distances()` now returns an immutable `IntSquareMatrix`.
- Updated [`FloydWarshall.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/024_floyd_warshall/FloydWarshall.java#L1-L66) to consume the immutable matrix directly and keep array handling internal.
- Simplified [`FloydWarshallDemo.java`](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/024_floyd_warshall/FloydWarshallDemo.java#L1-L22) so it just prints the result matrix object.

Why this is better:
- The public API no longer leaks raw mutable arrays.
- Formatting logic moved into the matrix type instead of the demo.
- Graph and result objects now expose immutable domain values rather than implementation details.

Verification:
